```sql
--Description:
--  Thinking process:
--    The previous joins showed no overlap between proteome aliquot IDs and
--    RNA-seq sample barcodes.  Before giving up on a transcriptome ↔ proteome
--    integration route, we should ask whether RNA-seq barcodes appear anywhere
--    in PDC’s global FILE-ASSOCIATED ENTITY mapping table.  That mapping lists
--    every entity_submitter_id (aliquot, sample, or case) referenced by any
--    PDC file, and could provide an alternative bridge (e.g., via “sample” or
--    “case” entities) even if aliquot IDs do not match.
--    This single query:
--      1. Extracts distinct “sample_barcode” values from the RNA-seq table.
--      2. Extracts distinct “entity_submitter_id” values from the
--         FILE_ASSOCIATED_ENTITY_MAPPING_CURRENT table.
--      3. Counts how many RNA-seq barcodes are present in that global mapping.
--    A non-zero result would indicate that we can pursue a two-step linkage
--    (RNA-seq sample → entity mapping → other PDC data sets).  A zero confirms
--    that RNA-seq sample barcodes are isolated from the file-entity universe,
--    and a different identifier (e.g., case_barcode) must be explored instead.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "rnaseq_vs_file_mapping_overlap"
FROM (
        SELECT DISTINCT "sample_barcode"
        FROM CPTAC_PDC.CPTAC.RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_CURRENT
     ) r
INNER JOIN (
        SELECT DISTINCT "entity_submitter_id"
        FROM CPTAC_PDC.PDC_METADATA.FILE_ASSOCIATED_ENTITY_MAPPING_CURRENT
     ) f
ON r."sample_barcode" = f."entity_submitter_id";
```
